# Repository attributes.
#
# WHITESPACE POLICY FOR CAPTURED MIGRATION EVIDENCE
#
# The capture directories under `docs/migration/smoke-evidence/` hold recorded evidence
# for the Java 17 / Node 20 runtime migration: server log regions mined verbatim out of a
# container log, HTTP response bodies and headers recorded byte for byte, unit-test report
# XML harvested from the test runner's own output, probe transcripts, and digest records.
# Those bytes ARE the evidence.  Trailing whitespace, a blank final line and
# space-before-tab inside them are part of what the observed tool actually emitted, so
# normalising them would edit the observation rather than tidy the repository -- and it
# would invalidate the SHA-256 manifests computed over these files and the
# baseline-against-migrated mirror diff that the evidence contract is built on.
#
# The `-whitespace` attribute below therefore disables git's whitespace checks for
# recorded capture output and for nothing else.  THE SCOPE IS CHOSEN BY MEASUREMENT, NOT
# BY CONVENIENCE, and it was re-measured over the whole change set: `git diff --check`
# reports violations in exactly four places -- the two side-by-side archives `baseline/`
# and `migrated/`, the reference-stack capture `provisioned-stack/`, and the single
# recorded transcript `activation-mime/results.txt`.  Each is listed, and nothing else is.
#
# HAND-WRITTEN FILES THAT SIT INSIDE A CAPTURE DIRECTORY STAY CHECKED.  A directory-wide
# exemption would otherwise absorb them silently, so the two hand-written files under
# `provisioned-stack/` -- its README and its analysis helper -- have the default checks
# restored by name immediately after the directory rule.  `activation-mime/` is exempted
# at the single recorded file rather than at the directory, because its probe source, its
# probe script and its notes are hand-written and must stay checked.
#
# Everything else in the repository keeps git's default whitespace checks, including every
# Java, XML, YAML, JSON, JavaScript, Python, shell and Markdown file, and including the
# capture scripts that sit one level above the captures -- `smoke-checks.sh`,
# `capture-static-audit.sh`, `install-surefire-evidence.sh`,
# `historical-frontend/capture-historical-frontend.sh`, `advisory-corpus/*.sh` -- which
# are clean on their own merits.
#
# The intended result is that `git diff --check <base>..HEAD` reports ZERO violations:
# hand-written files are clean because they are clean, and recorded bytes are exempt rather
# than rewritten.  If a violation ever appears in a hand-written file, the file is what
# should change; this policy must not be widened to absorb it.  That rule has already been
# applied once rather than merely stated: a blank line carrying twelve spaces in
# `AngularResourceCopier.java` was the one hand-written violation the re-measurement found,
# and the line was cleaned instead of the policy being widened to cover Java source.
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/baseline/** -whitespace
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/migrated/** -whitespace
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/provisioned-stack/** -whitespace
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/provisioned-stack/README.md !whitespace
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/provisioned-stack/extract-blocking-chain.py !whitespace
docs/migration/smoke-evidence/activation-mime/results.txt -whitespace
